source: crates/hibi-cli/tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "help(&repo, &[command, \"--help\"])"
---
$ hibi triage --help
exit status: 0
---- standard output ----
Ask the judge model which uncovered sentences, list items, table rows and headings state a fact that could be confirmed by reading code or configuration, and where the evidence would be. The result is a ranking to read, not a finding: nothing is written to the store.

Needs TYPESAFE_API_KEY and git. The text of the listed units is sent to the judge service. Only files that git tracks, or that are untracked and not ignored, are sent.

Usage: hibi triage [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --scope <name>
          Consider only this scope. Repeat for several [default: every scope]

      --since <range>
          Consider only units that were added or changed since a commit. The range is written as for `hibi status --since`

      --limit <n>
          Print at most this many units; 0 prints all
          
          [default: 50]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --root <dir>
          Use this directory as the root (the directory that contains .hibi/) instead of searching upward from the working directory

      --format <format>
          Output format. Without this option the output is JSON when standard output is not a terminal, and text when it is

          Possible values:
          - human: Text for a person
          - json:  One JSON object

      --now <timestamp>
          Use this instant as the current time, for reproducible runs. RFC 3339 with any offset, for example 2026-11-20T18:04:11Z. A fraction of a second is dropped

      --no-cache
          Do not read or write the cache database. Results are the same with and without the cache
---- standard error ----
